        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/garden_utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Garden sits at a high elevation of approximately 6,660 feet, placing it in close proximity to the freshwater Bear Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/garden_utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Loamy soils in Garden are well-suited for farming crops such as hay and grains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/garden_utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Garden is located within the Bear River watershed, where the river's northward flow historically contributed to local sediment deposition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/garden_utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The high elevation of Garden leads to cooler temperatures and increased precipitation compared to lower valleys.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
